+published under the fresh manifest before broader fan-out. The completed
+864-trial Gradient Boosting pilot selected both `l2_regularization=10` and
+`max_iter=600` at their upper boundaries. Its versioned follow-up retains every
+prior value and extends regularization through 100 and 1,000 and iteration caps
+through 1,200 and 2,400. The resulting 2,160 trials should be budgeted for at
+least 50 hours at the prior observed pace. These are development-only pilot
+measurements, not task time limits; detached workers may run for days when the
+manifest remains scientifically admissible.
 
 The largest four-year inner-fold preparation retains approximately 1.1 GiB of
 float32 tensor payload before masks, targets, and temporary numerical-library
diff --git a/logs/RESEARCH_LOG.md b/logs/RESEARCH_LOG.md
index ec33a00..eb6e912 100644
--- a/logs/RESEARCH_LOG.md
+++ b/logs/RESEARCH_LOG.md
@@ -940,3 +940,20 @@
   never be approved or fanned out; after this worker reaches terminal evidence,
   a fresh manifest must bind the corrected source and rerun exactly the four
   resource pilots before broader Stage A.
+
+## 2026-07-30
+
+- The superseded `taq5m-dev-v3-stagea-2469f2f` Gradient Boosting pilot
+  completed all 864 trials with no failed trial. Its best inner
+  target-balanced MSE was `0.5647586`, but the selected
+  `l2_regularization=10` and `max_iter=600` were both upper search-boundary
+  values. The task correctly published `SEARCH_EXPANSION_REQUIRED` and never
+  opened outer validation. This diagnosis uses development inner-CV evidence
+  only; no candidate, final-holdout, tensor outer, or Stage B economic result
+  was accessed.
+- Expanded the Gradient Boosting grid while retaining every prior value.
+  Regularization is now `[0, 1, 10, 100, 1000]`, and iteration caps are
+  `[50, 100, 300, 600, 1200, 2400]`, making both prior winners interior
+  choices. The full search contains 2,160 trials and 34,560 inner target-head
+  fits. Protocol validation and tests bind the expansion so a future manifest
+  cannot silently regress to the known incomplete search.
diff --git a/src/microstructure_veer/tournament/contracts.py b/src/microstructure_veer/tournament/contracts.py
index 9d77246..a8d5df7 100644
--- a/src/microstructure_veer/tournament/contracts.py
+++ b/src/microstructure_veer/tournament/contracts.py
@@ -406,14 +406,37 @@ class TournamentProtocol:
         if self.trial_budget("gradient_boosting") < 100:
             raise SafetyError("gradient boosting requires at least 100 configurations")
         gradient_space = self.family_space("gradient_boosting")
+        gradient_l2 = tuple(
+            float(value) for value in gradient_space.get("l2_regularization", ())
+        )
+        gradient_caps = tuple(
+            int(value) for value in gradient_space.get("max_iter", ())
+        )
         if (
             len(tuple(gradient_space.get("learning_rate", ()))) < 3
-            or len(tuple(gradient_space.get("max_iter", ()))) < 3
+            or len(gradient_caps) < 3
             or gradient_space.get("early_stopping") is not False
         ):
             raise SafetyError(
                 "gradient boosting requires interior learning-rate and iteration choices"
             )
+        if (
+            not gradient_l2
+            or not all(math.isfinite(value) for value in gradient_l2)
+            or gradient_l2 != tuple(sorted(set(gradient_l2)))
+            or gradient_l2[0] < 0.0
+            or 10.0 not in gradient_l2
+            or not any(value > 10.0 for value in gradient_l2)
+            or not gradient_caps
+            or gradient_caps != tuple(sorted(set(gradient_caps)))
+            or gradient_caps[0] < 1
+            or 600 not in gradient_caps
+            or not any(value > 600 for value in gradient_caps)
+        ):
+            raise SafetyError(
+                "gradient boosting must retain and expand beyond the "
+                "dev-2020 l2 and iteration boundary winners"
+            )
         for family in ("cp", "tucker"):
             if self.trial_budget(family) < 100:
                 raise SafetyError(f"{family} requires at least 100 configurations")
